    "updated_at": "2021-04-04T22:52:43Z",
    "body": "not sure if this is the right thread to resurrect for this, but i'm wondering if there's any mileage in allowing indeterminate to be set using an actual attribute in HTML? i.e. being able to (statically) set an checkbox to be `<input type=\"checkbox\" indeterminate>`, to match the same way this can be done but only for assistive technologies with `<input type=\"checkbox\" aria-checked=\"mixed\">`? again, it feels odd that it's possible to express this semantic concept in markup, but only for AT.",
